#heading(level: 2)[#text("What was checked")]

#text("Seven draft protocols passed the repository checker before freezing. The 35 Python sources in the seven prepared packages and two partial F1 sources were parsed with AST without importing their mathematical programs. Seven negative software fixtures confirm that absent/mismatched releases and changed protocol bytes fail before invoking a checkpoint process. Those are software checks, not real S3 gate passes. All eight preparation PDFs, nine pages total, were rendered with text-preserving compaction and visually inspected.")
#parbreak()

#text("The new static mathematics is retained in theory-before-data.md and each track's derivation/source notes. In particular, one-anchor pole-three sampling has an exact rational-slope law and structured path incidence; it does not justify a random-graph collision model. The cover's infinity-difference class has zero norm but is nonzero, so matching norms cannot certify class equality. The lattice's two-summand capacity scale is distinguished from the earlier three-summand bound. These are scoped derivations, not new measured rates.")
#parbreak()

#heading(level: 2)[#text("What blocks execution")]

#text("The current repository rule requires an actual S3 resume checkpoint before runs. Automatic approval review rejected the attempted upload because specific disclosure consent was required. The explicit owner question remains pending; no upload occurred and no skip path was used. Read-only configuration checks also found no supported checkpoint upload token or AWS CLI/profile/key pair. Approval and a configured transport are both necessary before the real gate.")
#parbreak()

#text("F1 has an additional platform halt recorded in environment/agent-halts-01.json; the coordinator's later capacity error is operational too. The partial F1 source is preserved byte-for-byte and its previous depth-four outcomes remain unknown. No missing execution is represented as an empty solution set.")
#parbreak()

